> Serves 4.

Finely chop @garlic{2%cloves} and finely slice @red chilli{2}. Thinly slice @spring onion{5} and @Lebanese cucumber{2}(halved). Roughly chop @roasted peanut{40%g}. Grate @ginger{1%tsp}.

== Beef Skewers ==

In a large bowl, combine @soy sauce{70%ml}, @honey{40%g}, sesame oil, the grated ginger, and black pepper until combined. Cut @beef rump{1%kg} into 4 cm cubes, add to the marinade, and toss to coat. Marinate for at least ~{15%minutes} at room temperature, or cover and refrigerate for up to ~{2%hours}.

Thread the marinated beef onto skewers. Grill on high heat for ~{8%minutes}, turning occasionally, until cooked to your liking. Sprinkle with @black sesame seeds{1%tsp}.

== Vermicelli Noodle Salad ==

Cook @vermicelli noodle{200%g} according to package instructions. Rinse under cold water to cool, then drain.

In a serving bowl, combine the noodles, chopped peanuts, @bean sprout{100%g}, @fresh mint{1%bunch}, @fresh coriander{1%bunch}, cucumber, and spring onion. Toss to combine.

== Nuoc Cham ==

Dissolve @caster sugar{1.5%tbsp} in hot water. Stir in the juice of @lime{2}, @fish sauce{45%ml}, garlic, and chilli.

Pour the nuoc cham over the noodle salad. Serve the skewers alongside the salad, garnished with extra sesame seeds, crushed peanuts, and a squeeze of fresh lime.
